      {
        "text": "Estuardo Mazariegos is a community organizer in South L.A. and a co-director of the Los Angeles office of the Alliance of Californians for Community Empowerment. He supports reducing the police budget and prioritizing basic services.",
        "cites": [1, 2],
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "Estuardo Mazariegos is a community organizer in South L.A. and a co-director of the Los Angeles office of the Alliance of Californians for Community Empowerment.",
            "cites": [1]
          },
          {
            "text": "He supports reducing the police budget and prioritizing basic services.",
            "cites": [2]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "On housing, he supports expanding social housing and enforcing tenant protections. He proposes auditing homeless services and raising wages, and wants to hire local youth for cleanups. He also backs a surcharge on event tickets to fund local businesses and parks. His campaign says he helped pass Measure ULA, along with the Tenant Anti-Harassment Ordinance and the Resident Protection Ordinance. In 2009, he pleaded guilty to a misdemeanor gun possession charge, and he has a shoplifting conviction.",
